.TH ZERODDS-GRPC-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-grpc-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/grpc-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the gRPC bridge daemon exposes DDS topics as gRPC
services. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-grpc-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/grpc-bridge/src/bridge_daemon/config.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " grpc ", " auth ", " metrics ", " topics ", " tenants .
.PP
An unknown key in a known section and a value of the wrong type or outside
its range stop the start with file and line (exit 1). An unknown top-level
key is a WARN line on stderr, and an error under
.BR \-\-check\-config .
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error ,
default
.IR info :
the threshold of the JSON log on stdout. A finished call is an
.I rpc
line at info (OK) or warn (any other status). A
.B \-\-log\-level
on the command line wins over this key.
.SS grpc
.TP
.B bind
HTTP/2 listen address, default
.IR "0.0.0.0:50051" .
Cleartext h2c (\fBtls.enabled: false\fR) only on a loopback address
(127.0.0.0/8, ::1, localhost); another address with TLS off stops the start
with exit 1, and \fB\-\-check\-config\fR refuses it.
.TP
.B max_concurrent_streams
1 to 2^32\-1, default
.IR 1024 .
The server's SETTINGS_MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS; a stream opened while that
many are open is refused with RST_STREAM(REFUSED_STREAM).
.TP
.B max_recv_message_size
Octets, default
.IR 4194304 .
A request message whose length prefix names more ends its call with
.I RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED
(8), then RST_STREAM(NO_ERROR) when the client still sends.
.TP
.B max_send_message_size
Octets, default
.IR 4194304 .
A larger response message ends a unary call, or a
.B Subscribe
stream, with
.IR RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED .
.TP
.B initial_window_size
1 to 2^31\-1, default
.IR 1048576 .
The server's SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE; a WINDOW_UPDATE opens the
connection window to the same size, and the server returns what a client
sent once half a window is used. A value below 65535 applies to a stream
once the client acknowledged the server's SETTINGS (RFC 9113 \(sc6.9.3).
.TP
.B max_frame_size
16384 to 16777215, default
.IR 16384 .
The server's SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE; a larger frame ends the connection.
.TP
.B keepalive
Sub-map with
.B time_secs
(default
.IR 60 ):
a PING after this long without a frame from the client, while a call is
open;
.B timeout_secs
(default
.IR 10 ):
GOAWAY and close when the PING is not acknowledged within it;
.B permit_without_calls
(default
.IR false ):
with false, the fourth client PING while no call is open (no HEADERS or
DATA of the server in between) ends the connection with
GOAWAY(ENHANCE_YOUR_CALM), and a connection without a call is closed after
5 s without a frame; with true every PING is answered and an idle
connection is kept by the server's PINGs.
.TP
.B drain_secs
0 to 300, default
.IR 30
(\(sc9.2). At SIGTERM or SIGINT every connection gets GOAWAY(NO_ERROR) with
the last stream the client opened; the calls up to it run on and end as
they do (a Subscribe stream delivers until the client ends it), a stream
opened after it is refused with RST_STREAM(REFUSED_STREAM). Calls still open
after
.B drain_secs
end with UNAVAILABLE. Within the same time the daemon waits for the
acknowledgements of its DDS writes, then deletes its DDS entities and exits
0. The systemd unit allows 40 s (TimeoutStopSec); a longer drain needs it
raised.
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean) and the server material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file ,
PEM, readable by user
.IR zerodds .
ALPN is
.I h2
for gRPC and
.I http/1.1
for the IDL endpoint.
.B client_ca_file
names the CA for client certificates;
.B require_client_cert
(boolean, default false) makes a client without a certificate fail the
handshake.
.B alpn
(list, default
.IR "[h2, http/1.1]" )
is what the listener offers in ALPN, in its order of preference; it names
.I h2
and may name
.IR http/1.1 ;
another entry, an entry named twice or a list without
.I h2
stops the start.
.B min_version
.RI ( 1.2 " | " 1.3 ,
default
.IR 1.2 )
is the lowest TLS version the listener accepts; TLS 1.3 is negotiated when
the client offers it.
.B cipher_suites
(list of IANA names, e.g.
.IR TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ;
without the key every suite of the crypto provider of the build) are the
suites offered, the first named preferred; a name the build does not offer
(in a FIPS build the suites outside FIPS 140-3), a name given twice, an
empty list, or a list
without a suite of a version from
.B min_version
up stops the start (exit 1, also under
.BR \-\-check\-config ).
With
.B enabled
and no
.BR cert_file / key_file ,
or material that does not load, the daemon does not start (exit 4).
.TP
.B reflection
Sub-map with
.BR enabled .
Turns on the reflection service
.RI ( grpc.reflection.v1 " and " grpc.reflection.v1alpha ):
it lists the topic services and serves the file descriptor of each package
(the messages and services of the generated definition), so that
.I "grpcurl describe"
and calls built from reflection work. The admin
.I /catalog
mirrors the same topic set.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls " (\(sc7.2),"
checked on every call; a failed check is
.IR UNAUTHENTICATED .
A mode whose input is missing stops the start.
.I none
only on a loopback
.B grpc.bind
(127.0.0.0/8, ::1, localhost); on another address it stops the start
(exit 1), also with TLS. SIGHUP checks it against the
.B grpc.bind
the listener serves (a changed bind needs a restart): a file that moves the
bind to loopback and sets
.I none
is refused, and the live auth settings stay.
.TP
.BR bearer_token ", " bearer_subject
For
.IR bearer :
the token in the
.I authorization
metadata
.RI ( "Bearer <token>" )
and the subject it stands for (default
.IR anonymous ).
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file: an RSA key, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, for RS256; a P-256
SubjectPublicKeyInfo for ES256; the token's
.I alg
has to be the key's algorithm),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim.
.PP
For
.IR mtls ,
.B grpc.tls.enabled
and
.B grpc.tls.client_ca_file
are required; the subject is the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514,
such as
.IR CN=alice,O=Example );
an ACL entry may name its fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address, an IP address and port (IPv6 in brackets). Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9095"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision. A host name such as
.I localhost:9095
stops the start with exit 1, and
\fB\-\-check\-config\fR refuses it.
.TP
.B path
The path of the Prometheus page, default
.IR /metrics ;
absolute, and none of
.IR / ", " /catalog ", " /healthz .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
The type name the DDS endpoints register (default
.IR ZeroDdsBridgeBytes ).
.TP
.B grpc_service
Name of the generated gRPC service, a protobuf identifier. Default: the
topic name split at
.I ::
(and at every character that is not an ASCII letter or digit), each part
capitalized, with the suffix
.I Stream
.RI ( Chat::Message " \(-> " ChatMessageStream ).
A dotted value is
.IR <package>.<Service> .
.TP
.B grpc_package
The protobuf package of the service. Default
.IR zerodds.<first\ part\ in\ lower\ case>.v1
.RI ( zerodds.chat.v1 ).
A call that names a package has to name this one; a call without the
package is NOT_FOUND when entries in several packages have its service
name; two entries of one fully-qualified service stop the start.
.TP
.B keyed
Whether
.B dds_type
declares a key, default
.IR true :
the topic's DataWriter and DataReaders are WITH_KEY endpoints, with
.I false
NO_KEY endpoints, as a DDS peer of a type without a key matches them;
a Sample with a key_hash on such a topic is INVALID_ARGUMENT.
.TP
.B idl_file
The IDL file that declares
.BR dds_type ,
read at the start; a file that cannot be read stops it. The daemon serves
its text at
.BI /idl/ <dds_name>
as
.I text/x-omg-idl
(HTTP/1.1 on the cleartext listener and, with ALPN
.I http/1.1
or none, on the TLS listener; an HTTP/2 GET on any connection), and
the
.B Catalog
call names that URL in
.IR idl_url .
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map:
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ;
default reliable; a best-effort
.B Subscribe
stream drops what its DataReader holds while 256 KiB wait for the client's
window, counted in
.I zerodds_grpc_bridge_samples_dropped_total
and logged at warn as
.IR samples_dropped ,
at most once a second per stream),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local " | " transient " | " persistent ;
default volatile; with one other than volatile the daemon retains the last
.B history.depth
samples per instance (all with keep_all or without a depth), at most
10000 of all such topics together, and sends them as
.IR SubscribeReq.initial_burst ,
followed without a gap by the live samples),
.B history
(a map of
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all )
and
.BR depth :
with keep_last the depth of the DataWriter that carries
.B Publish
calls into DDS, without a depth the runtime's default; with keep_all
that DataWriter keeps every sample, and a
.B depth
beside it is refused),
.B deadline_ms
(the deadline the writer offers and each stream's reader requests; a
.B Subscribe
stream ends with the trailer
.IR zerodds-deadline-missed ),
.B lifespan_ms
(the lifespan of the topic's DataWriter; a
.B Publish
with the metadata
.I zerodds-lifespan-ms
or a
.I grpc-timeout
writes with a DataWriter of that lifespan; at most 8 of them per topic, a
ninth lifespan takes the place of the one that wrote least recently once
its readers acknowledged it, on a durable topic only of one whose last
sample expired, else RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED).
Both 1 to 2147483647 milliseconds.
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries
.B Publish
calls into DDS (the daemon creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to
.B Subscribe
calls (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
A call against the direction a topic does not carry ends with
.B FAILED_PRECONDITION
(9); a failed DDS write with
.B UNAVAILABLE
(14).
.TP
.B acl
Sub-map with
.B publish
and
.B subscribe
(lists of subjects,
.I *
for all,
.I *group:<g>*
for a JWT group), \(sc7.3.
.B Publish
needs
.BR publish ,
.B Subscribe
needs
.BR subscribe ;
otherwise the call is
.IR PERMISSION_DENIED .
Without any
.B acl
every topic is open under
.BI "auth.mode: " none
and closed under every other mode; with one, a topic without an entry is
closed.
.SS tenants (list)
Each entry is a DDS participant of its own (\(sc1 L6).
A connection is bound to a tenant by its client certificate, so
.B tenants
needs
.BR grpc.tls.enabled " and " grpc.tls.client_ca_file ;
without them the start stops with a configuration error.
.TP
.B name
Unique, without
.IR / .
In the ACL and in the metric labels its topics and services are
.IR <name>/<dds_name> " and " <name>/<grpc_service> .
.TP
.B domain
Its DDS domain; default the top-level
.BR domain .
.TP
.B subjects
The client certificates bound to it: the subject DN (RFC 4514, such as
.IR CN=plant-a,O=Example )
or the fingerprint
.IR mtls:<SHA-256 hex> .
A TLS connection with such a certificate addresses the tenant's topics for
its whole life; a cleartext connection and one no tenant names address the
top-level
.BR topics .
A subject is bound to one tenant at most.
.TP
.B topics
As the top-level
.BR topics .
.PP
A changed
.BR tenants
entry, limit,
.BR keepalive " or " drain_secs
setting or
.B path
needs a restart; SIGHUP applies TLS material, auth and ACL.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/grpc-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged (1).
